                        "# Scaling Strategies\n\n## Vertical Scaling (Scale Up)\nAdd more power to existing machine.\n```\nBefore: 4 CPU, 16GB RAM\nAfter:  32 CPU, 256GB RAM\n```\n**Pros:** Simple, no code changes\n**Cons:** Hardware limits, single point of failure\n\n## Horizontal Scaling (Scale Out)\nAdd more machines.\n```\nBefore: 1 server\nAfter:  10 servers behind load balancer\n```\n**Pros:** Nearly unlimited scale, fault tolerance\n**Cons:** Complex, needs stateless design\n\n## When to Choose\n```\nVertical: Database servers, legacy apps, < 10K users\nHorizontal: Web servers, microservices, > 100K users\nHybrid: Most production systems\n```\n\n## Auto-Scaling (AWS)\n```yaml\nAutoScalingGroup:\n  MinSize: 2\n  MaxSize: 20\n  TargetTrackingPolicy:\n    TargetValue: 70  # CPU utilization %\n    PredefinedMetricSpecification:\n      PredefinedMetricType: ASGAverageCPUUtilization\n```",
