                        "# Message Queues\n\n## When to Use\n```\n✓ Decouple producers from consumers\n✓ Handle traffic spikes (buffer)\n✓ Ensure reliable delivery\n✓ Enable async processing\n✓ Fan-out to multiple consumers\n```\n\n## Kafka Architecture\n```\nProducer → Topic (partitioned) → Consumer Group\n\nTopic: orders\n  Partition 0: [msg1, msg4, msg7, ...]\n  Partition 1: [msg2, msg5, msg8, ...]\n  Partition 2: [msg3, msg6, msg9, ...]\n\nConsumer Group A:\n  Consumer 1 reads Partition 0\n  Consumer 2 reads Partition 1,2\n\nConsumer Group B (independent):\n  Consumer 3 reads all partitions\n```\n\n## Python + Kafka\n```python\nfrom kafka import KafkaProducer, KafkaConsumer\nimport json\n\n# Producer\nproducer = KafkaProducer(\n    bootstrap_servers='localhost:9092',\n    value_serializer=lambda v: json.dumps(v).encode()\n)\n\nproducer.send('orders', {\n    'order_id': '12345',\n    'user_id': 'u789',\n    'total': 99.99,\n    'items': ['widget_a', 'widget_b']\n})\nproducer.flush()\n\n# Consumer\nconsumer = KafkaConsumer(\n    'orders',\n    bootstrap_servers='localhost:9092',\n    group_id='order-processor',\n    value_deserializer=lambda m: json.loads(m.decode())\n)\n\nfor message in consumer:\n    order = message.value\n    process_order(order)\n    print(f'Processed order {order[\"order_id\"]}')\n```\n\n## RabbitMQ vs Kafka vs SQS\n```\nRabbitMQ: Traditional queue, message routing, small-medium scale\nKafka: Event streaming, replay, high throughput, big data\nSQS: Managed AWS, serverless, no ops, auto-scale\nRedis Streams: Lightweight, in-memory, good for real-time\n```",
