                        "# Notification System\n\n## Types\n```\nPush: Mobile notifications (APNs, FCM)\nSMS: Text messages (Twilio, AWS SNS)\nEmail: Transactional + marketing (SendGrid, SES)\nIn-App: Real-time UI updates (WebSocket)\n```\n\n## Architecture\n```\nEvent Source → Kafka → Notification Service → Channel Router\n                                                  ├→ Push (APNs/FCM)\n                                                  ├→ Email (SES)\n                                                  ├→ SMS (Twilio)\n                                                  └→ In-App (WebSocket)\n```\n\n## Rate Limiting & Deduplication\n```python\nclass NotificationService:\n    def __init__(self, redis_client):\n        self.redis = redis_client\n    \n    async def send(self, user_id: str, notification: dict):\n        # Deduplication (idempotency key)\n        dedup_key = f'notif:{notification[\"id\"]}'\n        if await self.redis.exists(dedup_key):\n            return  # Already sent\n        \n        # Rate limit: max 10 notifications per hour\n        rate_key = f'rate:{user_id}:notif'\n        count = await self.redis.incr(rate_key)\n        if count == 1:\n            await self.redis.expire(rate_key, 3600)\n        if count > 10:\n            return  # Rate limited\n        \n        # Check user preferences\n        prefs = await self.get_preferences(user_id)\n        if not prefs.get(notification['channel'], True):\n            return  # User opted out\n        \n        # Send via channel\n        await self.dispatch(user_id, notification)\n        await self.redis.setex(dedup_key, 86400, '1')\n```",
